<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>hwnhub — a Flatpak channel</title>
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
    body {
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
      max-width: 42rem;
      margin: 3rem auto;
      padding: 0 1.25rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }
    h1 { font-size: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
    h1 + p { color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 65%, transparent); margin-top: 0; }
    h2 { margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: 1.15rem; }
    .app {
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      padding: 0.75rem 0;
      border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 15%, transparent);
    }
    .app:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 15%, transparent); }
    .app-name { font-weight: 600; }
    .app-version {
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 60%, transparent);
      font-size: 0.9em;
    }
    .app-ref { margin-left: auto; font-size: 0.9em; }
    code, pre {
      font-family: ui-monospace, "JetBrains Mono", "SF Mono", Consolas, monospace;
      font-size: 0.9em;
    }
    pre {
      background: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 8%, transparent);
      padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
      border-radius: 6px;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }
    a { color: inherit; }
    .empty { color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 60%, transparent); font-style: italic; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>hwnhub</h1>
  <p>A self-hosted Flatpak channel for hawwwran's apps.</p>

  <h2>Apps in this channel</h2>
  <div id="apps">
@APP_LIST@
  </div>

  <h2>Adding the channel by hand</h2>
  <p>Clicking any <code>.flatpakref</code> above does this for you. If you'd rather use the CLI:</p>
  <pre><code>flatpak remote-add --if-not-exists hwnhub \
  https://hawwwran.github.io/hwnhub/hwnhub.flatpakrepo</code></pre>

  <h2>What is this?</h2>
  <p>
    Same mechanics as Flathub, smaller scale. Once you've installed one app from
    here, GNOME Software shows updates for it and any other app in this channel
    on its normal refresh cadence. The repo is GPG-signed; the public key is
    bundled into every <code>.flatpakref</code>, so trust is established at
    install time.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top: 3rem; font-size: 0.85em; color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 50%, transparent);">
    Tooling lives at <a href="https://github.com/hawwwran/hwnhub">github.com/hawwwran/hwnhub</a>.
  </p>
</body>
</html>
